+# Experimental startup thinking provenance
+
+**Local investigation only. Not an official supported Pi release. Ticket 01 remains BLOCKED.**
+
+This checkout experiments with one additive field on `SessionStartEvent`. It does not integrate Jev into Pi, change thinking precedence, or change session persistence. Production repositories and installed packages remain untouched.
+
+## Proposed contract
+
+```typescript
+interface SessionStartEvent {
+  type: "session_start";
+  reason: "startup" | "reload" | "new" | "resume" | "fork";
+  previousSessionFile?: string;
+  thinkingLevelOverride?: ThinkingLevel;
+}
+```
+
+`createAgentSession()` supplies `thinkingLevelOverride` from its explicit `options.thinkingLevel`, before model-capability clamping. `undefined` means that runtime creation had no explicit thinking option; it does not mean `"off"`. Settings and transcript values are never used to infer the field. The SDK overwrites any caller-supplied provenance in `sessionStartEvent` with the real option.
+
+The CLI passes its resolved startup thinking option through that SDK factory for each runtime creation/replacement. Runtime replacement (`new`, `resume`, `fork`, clone, import) therefore reports the option used by the replacement factory. A custom host must explicitly carry its option into its factory; this field does not make a prior option sticky.
+
+Reload is not runtime creation: its `session_start` event has reason `"reload"` and no override. It must not cause consumers to reapply an old startup option over a manual current choice. Tree navigation emits `session_tree`, not `session_start`; consumers should replay the active prefix rather than use startup precedence there. This is provenance of a creation input, not an instruction to reapply that input indefinitely.
+
+Consumers needing the effective selection must use the current host value or the public `clampThinkingLevel()` helper and current model. For example, raw `"max"` may select effective `"high"`; a non-reasoning model selects `"off"`. Do not infer source from equality between those values.
+
+## Why this seam
+
+A `message_start` thinking setter persists before its owning user. Fork-before can retain that provisional change while excluding its owner. Existing user `message_end` also precedes persistence. `context` runs after request thinking capture, while `before_provider_request` exposes opaque provider payloads. None is a supported provider-neutral fix in released Pi 1.3.0.
+
+Authoritative provenance lets a branch-aware consumer reconcile excluded applications only when the host restored history, while leaving explicit replacement choices authoritative. It retains the existing consumer's application/owner ledger. A post-user-persistence event could remove some of that ledger, but must still define fork-at boundaries (the owner can be included while later metadata is excluded), cancellation, and tree restoration. A request-local effort API avoids persistent provisional changes entirely, but needs explicit semantics for continuation, retries, queue batches, tool turns, manual changes, branch reconstruction, and displayed effort. Those are larger, useful alternatives, not implied by this one-field experiment.
+
+Existing public alternatives have different integration contracts. An SDK owner can install `session.agent.prepareRequest` (agent-core `PrepareRequest`), returning `{ thinkingLevel }` per request after persisted input, but an ordinary extension has no supported access to that callback. Using it requires a host-owned SDK wrapper, whose lifecycle and per-prompt decision semantics need approval. `registerVirtualModel().route(request, ctx)` already returns a provider-neutral physical model/thinking pair with a request signal. It requires selecting a virtual model and uses separate selection/dispatch state, so it does not preserve the current requirement to keep the user's physical model selection unchanged. Neither is silently substituted by this experiment.
+
+## Acceptance matrix (defined before tests)
+
+Sources: operator investigation task; ticket `docs/testing/ticket-01-startup-provenance-blocker.md`; independent fresh review of `917ec659422e05243d3eb66ab1d82f61f54c4bd6`; supervisor-approved local experiment. Expected values below are literal acceptance requirements, not computed from the implementation.
+
+| Criterion | Test ID / behavior | Independent expected observation |
+|---|---|---|
+| AC-1 | CLI-1: no override, fork-before excluded high owner | Restored state and next low/0-confidence generation are medium |
+| AC-2 | CLI-2: explicit startup high equals excluded provisional high after manual medium | Replacement state and next no-change generation remain high |
+| AC-3 | CLI-3: tree retains manual low on active prefix | State and next no-change generation are low |
+| AC-4 | CLI-4: reload after startup high and manual low | State and next no-change generation stay low, reload carries no creation override |
+| AC-5 | CLI-5: fork-at includes owner but not later receipt | High and reusable decision survive; continuation does not classify again |
+| AC-6 | CLI-6: steering and follow-up mode all, low lookup then continuation | Requests [high, high, low]; separate low classified/reused receipts with correct owner IDs |
+| AC-7 | CLI-7: abort active classifier, then submit fresh work | Classifier HTTP aborts, no generation/application/receipt for canceled classification; next work succeeds |
+| AC-8 | CLI-8: session effort changes | Global settings bytes remain unchanged |
+| AC-9 | CLI-9: explicit off differs from omitted override | Fork-before and no-change generation stay off |
+| AC-10 | CLI-10 / SDK-10: unsupported raw override | Raw max remains authoritative provenance; effective host/request high for restricted reasoning model, off for non-reasoning model |
+| AC-11 | CLI-11: new/resume/clone; SDK-11: import runtime producer | Each replacement reports its actual factory override and next request uses it |
+| AC-12 | SDK-12: equal SDK option vs no option, conflicting supplied metadata | Explicit high vs undefined distinguished at equal effective high; SDK option wins over supplied event metadata |
+| AC-13 | CLI-13: excluded application then ineligible input | Orphan application is closed, not reassigned to a future user |
+
+The consumer fixture is an experimental copy of ticket `a2ebf6f4ccc7a2f610c9340958203f6fbcdddede`, not a new production adapter. Only restoration consumes the new field; classification, pending ownership, and active signal handling stay on public APIs. CLI tests run the actual source CLI in RPC mode against local HTTP classifier/model servers. SDK tests use the faux provider. No credentials or paid inference are used.
+
+## Compatibility and rollout gate
+
+The field is additive, but optional absence on released hosts is indistinguishable from no override on an experimental host. A consumer must require a known released supporting host version/capability; silently feature-detecting this field on one event is insufficient. Direct `new AgentSession()` hosts must provide authoritative metadata themselves if they bypass the SDK. Other extensions may mutate thinking during startup; this field only identifies the SDK input and does not order arbitrary competing writers.
+
+This experiment does not migrate historical Jev ledgers or approve their adoption. Before any target change: independent review, operator approval of the seam/rollout, official host support or explicitly approved custom-host contract, and complete target CLI regressions are required. Interactive rendering, real Jev services, paid providers, and exhaustive cancellation timing interleavings are outside this local proof.
+
+## Source lifecycle map
+
+Paths below are relative to `packages/coding-agent/src`, except agent-core references. These are investigation-checkout line references, not claims about a future release.
+
+| Boundary | Source | Consequence |
+|---|---|---|
+| CLI startup option | `main.ts:475–546,818–857` | Explicit `--thinking`, model suffix, or resolved scoped startup level becomes `sessionOptions.thinkingLevel`; creation options are recalculated for replacement cwd/services |
+| SDK selection | `core/sdk.ts:253–278` | Explicit option outranks transcript; settings are fallback; model clamp follows |
+| SDK persistence | `core/sdk.ts:448–458` | Existing transcript with thinking metadata gets no new equal-value source marker |
+| New metadata | `core/sdk.ts:477–481`; `core/extensions/types.ts:755–766` | SDK creation records the raw option independently of effective value |
+| Initial event | `core/agent-session.ts:3288–3312` | Extension binding emits the prepared creation event |
+| User persistence | `core/agent-session.ts:1143–1168` | Extension `message_end` completes before `appendMessage()` assigns the user's persisted entry ID |
+| Capture | `core/agent-session.ts:785–846`; `packages/agent/src/agent-loop.ts:219–250` | Request projection reads selected thinking before stream/context transformation |
+| Context | `core/sdk.ts:436–439`; `packages/agent/src/agent-loop.ts:381–409` | Context transformation is later than thinking capture; changing session thinking there cannot rewrite captured config |
+| Session-local setter | `core/agent-session.ts:2642–2664` | Appends effective thinking on change; global defaults only with `persist: true` |
+| Replacement | `core/agent-session-runtime.ts:167–188,195–401` | Abort and teardown current session; create through stored factory, then bind replacement |
+| Reload | `core/agent-session.ts:3723–3727` | Emits `{ type: "session_start", reason: "reload" }` on the same session; no creation option reapplied |
+| Tree | `core/agent-session.ts:4118–4181` | Moves leaf and rebuilds messages/tools; does not restore thinking; consumer replays active prefix on `session_tree` |
+
+All replacement producers were checked: new (`runtime.ts:251`), resume (`:218`), fork with empty prefix (`:305`), persisted fork (`:326`), in-memory fork (`:345`), and JSONL import (`:397`). All converge on the SDK via the runtime factory. Clone uses fork-at; no separate provenance source is needed. Focused behavioral tests cover persisted fork-before/fork-at, new/resume/clone and SDK import. Empty-prefix and in-memory fork producer sites were inspected, not given new dedicated provenance E2E cases.
+
+The released public SDK already exposes agent-core `PrepareRequest` at `packages/agent/src/types.ts:173–189`. It returns `AgentRequestUpdate` (context/model/thinkingLevel), accepts the active `AbortSignal`, and runs after selected input events. This is a supported host-owner alternative, not an extension API. The existing virtual-model route contract is documented in `docs/virtual-models.md`; it changes selection semantics and was not prototyped.
+
+## Local validation and before/after proof
+
+Environment: Darwin arm64, Node `v26.8.1`, npm `11.19.0`. The host has `package-lock.json` and CI uses `npm ci --ignore-scripts`, so its npm manager was preserved instead of converting to Bun. Install used a new isolated `/tmp/pi-jev-host-api-npm-cache` with lifecycle scripts disabled. npm reported existing dependency engine/deprecation warnings; no manifests or lockfiles changed.
+
+The initial source CLI could not import ignored generated model data (`packages/ai/src/providers/data/amazon-bedrock.json`). Copying official installed Pi AI **1.3.0** model JSON read-only into this checkout's ignored data directory resolved it; `npm run check:model-data` passed. No build, downloaded model catalog, provider credentials or paid inference was needed. The original CLI path was reproduced before changing host or consumer.
+
+**RED, original host and unmodified consumer:**
+
+```text
+node ../../node_modules/vitest/dist/cli.js --run test/thinking-provenance-cli.test.ts -t CLI-2
+Tests 1 failed | 11 skipped
+                  expected   observed
+fork state        high       medium
+provider effort   high       medium
+receipt effective high       medium
+```
+
+SDK contract tests were also RED before implementation: supplied event metadata `low` was not derived from the actual absent SDK option; a high option on a non-reasoning model had no corresponding provenance field.
+
+**GREEN, host prototype and experimental consumer:**
+
+```sh
+# From packages/coding-agent
+node ../../node_modules/vitest/dist/cli.js --run \
+  test/thinking-provenance-cli.test.ts test/thinking-provenance-sdk.test.ts \
+  test/agent-session-runtime-events.test.ts test/suite/agent-session-runtime.test.ts \
+  test/sdk-session-manager.test.ts test/sdk-stream-options.test.ts \
+  test/suite/agent-session-model-extension.test.ts test/suite/agent-session-queue.test.ts
+```
+
+Result: **8 files, 79 tests passed**. The 16 new tests cover all 13 matrix criteria; the remaining 63 are existing lifecycle/runtime/SDK/model/queue regressions. This is actual source CLI/RPC/HTTP E2E and SDK/faux execution, not an installed-release or interactive-TUI claim. The equality case now asserts high in state, actual serialized provider request and retained receipt; no-override medium and manual-prefix low pass in the same run. Both all-mode queue variants assert `[high, high, low]`, three classifications and distinct correct receipt owner IDs.
+
+During test development, the abort assertion was corrected to exclude a legitimate pre-existing startup restore marker rather than prohibit all restore metadata. SDK fixtures were configured with faux provider auth. `/import` is not a built-in RPC prompt command, so import proof uses the public SDK runtime operation rather than pretending a normal user prompt exercised import. These were fixture corrections, not hidden product changes.
+
+Full check was decomposed with supervisor approval to avoid root `npm run check` invoking `biome --write .`. Only explicitly authored files were formatted; whole-repo Biome ran read-only:
+
+```sh
+node scripts/biome-check.mjs
+npm run check:pinned-deps
+npm run check:runtime-deps
+npm run check:ts-imports
+npm run check:entry-graphs
+npm run check:install-lock:coding-agent
+node node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc --noEmit
+npm run check:browser-smoke
+git diff --check
+```
+
+All passed; Biome checked **1492 files, no fixes applied**. The literal root `npm run check`, build, full test suite, package release and production target regressions were **not run**. This is not a claim that the literal root command ran. No staged files remain after the local investigation commit.
