+# Experimental Jev consumer fixture
+
+This is a throwaway acceptance consumer for the local host API investigation, not a supported Jev release, built-in extension, or production integration.
+
+The four consumer source files were copied from ticket checkout commit `a2ebf6f4ccc7a2f610c9340958203f6fbcdddede`:
+
+- `extension.ts`
+- `effort-policy.ts`
+- `system-one.ts`
+- `classifier-context.ts`
+
+Behavioral changes are restricted to `extension.ts`: replace value-equality provenance with the experimental `SessionStartEvent.thinkingLevelOverride` and treat reload/tree as active-prefix reconstruction, not runtime-creation override application. The fixture also types the local config variable and follows host Biome formatting/import ordering. Policy, transport, and minimized classifier context are not redesigned. Upstream attribution/license are preserved in `NOTICE.md` and `LICENSE`.
+
+`controls.ts` exposes supported command-context fork-at/tree/reload controls and records startup event metadata. `cli-fixture.ts` launches the actual checkout CLI with its source resolver, an isolated HOME/agent directory and explicit extensions. It only sends requests to loopback HTTP servers, never to real providers. Its fake model server speaks OpenAI-compatible SSE; assertions inspect actual serialized `reasoning_effort` after Pi's provider-neutral selection and model clamp.
+
+The source checkout needs generated model data for imports. In this investigation it was copied read-only from the already installed official `@earendil-works/pi-ai` 1.3.0 `dist/providers/data` to the ignored checkout `packages/ai/src/providers/data`, and `npm run check:model-data` validated it. No installed dependency, production checkout, existing dependency cache, manifest or lockfile was modified.
+
+See `../../../docs/experimental-thinking-provenance.md` for the proposed contract and pre-test acceptance matrix. Run from `packages/coding-agent`:
+
+```sh
+node ../../node_modules/vitest/dist/cli.js --run test/thinking-provenance-cli.test.ts test/thinking-provenance-sdk.test.ts
+```
